{# The float/SIMD section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# float/SIMD findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text, scan #}
{# coverage record) so each template passes its own heading text and the #}
{# coverage the producing scan stamped. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{# The coverage record (issue #347) arrives as CoverageInfo strings: the #}
{# scan's status word and its admission line. The include appends exactly #}
{# one "Coverage:" qualification line — beside the entries, or as the whole #}
{# section beside the heading when the scan stamped no findings but admits #}
{# falling short — whenever the record carries an admission; a complete or #}
{# missing record renders exactly what it rendered before, and the line #}
{# names only bodies the scan never reached, never an examined-and-clean #}
{# body the flag list left unmentioned. #}
{# The seam capability records (#357 fan-out): one admission line per #}
{# family this section feeds — the engine facets behind it, as the capability #}
{# probe answers them — quoted from the held seam report. Each rides exactly #}
{# one "Analysis engine:" line, after the coverage line, beside the entries; #}
{# when the section filed nothing at all the line rides under the heading, #}
{# the heading opening for the first line that needs it. An answerable or #}
{# undeclared family renders exactly what it rendered before. #}
{% macro floatsimd_section(findings, heading, coverage, decompilation_cap) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

This function's body carries float/SIMD evidence, recorded by static
analysis — the decompiler mangles vector math into concatenations,
extractions, and undefined-typed arithmetic, and reading it as integer
or pointer logic mistranslates it. Translate the math as float: for a
scalar shape use plain `f32`/`f64` operations; for a vector/matrix
shape use component arrays or small vector structs, never packed
integers:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** ({{ finding.kind }} shape, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% if !decompilation_cap.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
{% if coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
Analysis engine: {{ decompilation_cap }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
